  "id": "usable",
  "term": "usable",
  "definition": "In this context, usable means that a protection or support process can be practically accessed and carried through by disabled people in real conditions, not just offered in theory. A usable response works across steps such as disclosure, evidence, movement, and care so that barriers do not stop access to safety.",
